Usage: gwi gmail extract-attachments [OPTIONS] --archive-dir <PATH>

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Gmail account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Gmail account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066). Overrides `GWI_GMAIL_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `gmail` subtree — unlike `--profile` it is not usable before the `gmail` subcommand name, only after it (`gmail --account NAME <cmd>` or `gmail <cmd> --account NAME`), so it can't collide with another product's own `--account` flag (Drive has the same one) as more command trees are added.

      --archive-dir <PATH>
          Archive directory previously populated by `gmail sync`/`sync-all`

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --dry-run
          Reports which messages would gain extracted attachments without writing any file

      --quiet
          Only shows errors, suppresses the per-message action lines

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Report format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi gmail render =====
Renders one or more archived `.eml` files as human-readable Markdown (CLI-only; no MCP equivalent; purely local, no client/credentials needed; rust-works/omni-dev#1513)

Usage: gwi gmail render [OPTIONS] <PATH|--archive-dir <PATH>>

Arguments:
  [PATH]...
          One or more `.eml` file paths to render. Mutually exclusive with `--archive-dir`

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Gmail account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Gmail account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066). Overrides `GWI_GMAIL_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `gmail` subtree — unlike `--profile` it is not usable before the `gmail` subcommand name, only after it (`gmail --account NAME <cmd>` or `gmail <cmd> --account NAME`), so it can't collide with another product's own `--account` flag (Drive has the same one) as more command trees are added.

      --archive-dir <PATH>
          Archive directory previously populated by `gmail sync`/`sync-all`. Renders every non-deleted message from its `manifest.jsonl` selected by `--all`/`--since`/`--until`/`--id`/`--ids-from`/`--source-label` (see `selection`). Mutually exclusive with positional `PATH` arguments

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --all
          Selects every non-deleted archived message

      --since <DATE>
          Selects messages with an internal date on or after this UTC date (`YYYY-MM-DD`)

      --until <DATE>
          Selects messages with an internal date on or before this UTC date (`YYYY-MM-DD`), inclusive of the whole day

      --id <ID>
          Selects one specific archived message id. Repeatable

      --ids-from <FILE>
          Selects message ids listed one per line in FILE (`-` for stdin); blank lines and `#`-prefixed comments are skipped — the same shape a `--dry-run` report's ids can be piped back through

      --source-label <LABEL_ID>
          Selects messages carrying this Gmail label id in the archived manifest (a raw label id, e.g. `Label_1` — not the destination `--label` tag `gmail insert` itself applies)

      --out-dir <DIR>
          Writes one `.md` file per input (named after the input's stem) into this directory instead of printing Markdown to stdout. With `--archive-dir`, also makes a message already rendered by a prior run into this directory skipped on this run

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Report format. `Table` (default) prints each input's rendered Markdown directly to stdout — or, with `--out-dir`, a `Saved to:` line per file — so redirecting stdout to a file yields clean Markdown; json/yaml/yamls/jsonl instead emit one structured record per input

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

      --fold-quotes
          Collapses `>`-quoted reply history nested more than one level deep into a one-line `*(N quoted lines omitted)*` marker (rust-works/omni-dev#1514). Off by default: verbatim rendering is fully information-preserving, and the full text is one re-render away without this flag

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi gmail insert =====
Restores archived `.eml` messages into a mailbox (needs `gmail.modify`; CLI-only; no MCP equivalent; rust-works/omni-dev#1655)

Usage: gwi gmail insert [OPTIONS] --archive-dir <PATH>

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Gmail account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Gmail account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066). Overrides `GWI_GMAIL_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `gmail` subtree — unlike `--profile` it is not usable before the `gmail` subcommand name, only after it (`gmail --account NAME <cmd>` or `gmail <cmd> --account NAME`), so it can't collide with another product's own `--account` flag (Drive has the same one) as more command trees are added.

      --archive-dir <PATH>
          Archive directory previously populated by `gmail sync`/`sync-all`

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --all
          Selects every non-deleted archived message

      --since <DATE>
          Selects messages with an internal date on or after this UTC date (`YYYY-MM-DD`)

      --until <DATE>
          Selects messages with an internal date on or before this UTC date (`YYYY-MM-DD`), inclusive of the whole day

      --id <ID>
          Selects one specific archived message id. Repeatable

      --ids-from <FILE>
          Selects message ids listed one per line in FILE (`-` for stdin); blank lines and `#`-prefixed comments are skipped — the same shape a `--dry-run` report's ids can be piped back through

      --source-label <LABEL_ID>
          Selects messages carrying this Gmail label id in the archived manifest (a raw label id, e.g. `Label_1` — not the destination `--label` tag `gmail insert` itself applies)

      --limit <LIMIT>
          Caps how many selected messages are inserted, applied after selection to the oldest-first plan. `0` means no limit
          
          [default: 0]

      --label <NAME>
          Tags every inserted message with this label, resolved by name against the destination mailbox's existing labels. Never auto-created — since inserted mail's raw headers still name the *original* recipient, `to:` searches won't match it, making this tag the only reliable handle for "what came from the archive"

      --drop-label <LABEL_ID>
          Drops this label id from a message's replayed system-label set (applied after the system-label filter). Repeatable — e.g. `--drop-label INBOX --drop-label UNREAD` restores mail as already-read and archived rather than dumping it into a live Inbox

      --concurrency <CONCURRENCY>
          Bounds concurrent inserts. Clamped to `1..=gmail::messages_api::MAX_CONCURRENCY`
          
          [default: 4]

      --verify-remote
          Before inserting, probes the destination for a message already carrying the same `Message-ID` (`rfc822msgid:` search) and skips it on a hit. A supplement to the local ledger, not a substitute — the probe costs quota and a round-trip per message and can lag a recent insert by seconds to minutes; useful mainly for a first run into a mailbox that may already hold some of this mail, or as a recovery probe after losing the ledger

      --dry-run
          Reports what would be inserted without making any `messages.insert` call or writing the ledger

      --quiet
          Only shows errors, suppresses per-message action lines and the live progress bar

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Report format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi drive =====
Drive: search, read, edit and sync Google Drive files, plus Docs, Sheets and Slides

Usage: gwi drive [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  auth         Manages Drive OAuth2 credentials
  account      Manages named Drive accounts
  search       Searches Drive files
  read         Reads a single Drive file's metadata or content
  dedupe       Finds Drive files sharing the same content hash
  sync         Mirrors a Drive folder recursively to local disk (one-way, read-only scope)
  create       Creates a new file or folder, gated by the folder write-permission rules (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1574). Requires the `drive.file` or `drive` scope (`drive auth login --write-file`/`--write-full`)
  upload       Uploads local content as a new file, gated by the folder write-permission rules (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1574). Requires the `drive.file` or `drive` scope (`drive auth login --write-file`/`--write-full`)
  edit         Replaces an existing file's content, gated by the write-permission rules (issues rust-works/omni-dev#1574, rust-works/omni-dev#1612). Requires the `drive.file` scope if `gwi` created the file, or the unrestricted `drive` scope for any pre-existing file (`drive auth login --write-file` or `--write-full`)
  trash        Moves an individual file to Drive Trash, gated by `trash` permission. Refuses folders; lease-exempt. Requires `drive auth login --write`
  untrash      Restores an individual file from Drive Trash under `trash` permission. Refuses folders; lease-exempt. Requires `drive auth login --write`
  lease        Backs up a file and mints a Touch ID-authorised lease token, required by `drive edit` and (in later phases) every other content-mutating verb (ADR-0080)
  rename       Renames a single Drive file. Requires the `drive.metadata` scope (`drive auth login --write`)
  move         Moves one or more Drive files into a destination folder. Requires the `drive.metadata` scope (`drive auth login --write`)
  permissions  Inspects the write-permission rules gating `drive create`/`upload`/`edit`, `drive sheets write`/`append`/`clear`/`create` and `drive docs replace`/`append`/`create` (issues rust-works/omni-dev#1574, rust-works/omni-dev#1589, rust-works/omni-dev#1612, rust-works/omni-dev#1615)
  docs         Reads the structure and text of a Google Doc via the Docs v1 API (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1615)
  slides       Reads Slides objects and replaces text on ordinary slides
  sheets       Reads and writes the cells of a Google Sheet via the Sheets v4 API (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1589)
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

