      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --operation <OPERATION>
          Which operation to check

          Possible values:
          - read
          - create
          - upload
          - edit
          - sheets-write:      Writing cells into a Google Sheet — distinct from `Edit`, see [`DriveOperation::SheetsWrite`]
          - sheets-structure:  Structurally editing a Google Sheet — distinct from `SheetsWrite`, see [`DriveOperation::SheetsStructure`]
          - sheets-delete:     Destructively editing a Google Sheet — distinct from `SheetsStructure`, see [`DriveOperation::SheetsDelete`]
          - sheets-protection: Adding, changing or removing a protected range — distinct from `SheetsStructure`, see [`DriveOperation::SheetsProtection`]
          - docs-write:        Replacing or appending text in a Google Doc — distinct from both `Edit` and `SheetsWrite`, see [`DriveOperation::DocsWrite`]
          - trash:             Moving an individual file to Trash or restoring it
          - slides-write:      Replacing text on ordinary Slides pages
          - docs-delete:       Anchor-addressed content deletion; separate from docs-write
          - docs-format:       Anchor-addressed text and paragraph styling
          - docs-structure:    Add empty Docs tables, rows or columns, or change named-range metadata
          - docs-table-delete: Remove Docs table rows or columns

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi drive docs =====
Reads the structure and text of a Google Doc via the Docs v1 API (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1615)

Usage: gwi drive docs [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  info                         Shows a document's title, revision id and structural outline (mirrors the `drive_docs_info` MCP tool)
  read                         Reads a document's structural elements with their index ranges (mirrors the `drive_docs_read` MCP tool)
  replace                      Replaces every occurrence of some text, gated by the write-permission rules (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1615). Requires the `drive.file` or `drive` scope (`drive auth login --write-file`/`--write-full`). (mirrors the `drive_docs_replace` MCP tool)
  append                       Appends text to the end of a document, gated by the write-permission rules (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1615). (mirrors the `drive_docs_append` MCP tool)
  insert                       Inserts text before or after a unique body or segment anchor, gated by docs-write
  delete                       Deletes a unique match or inclusive anchor range, gated by docs-delete
  create-bullets               Creates bullets or numbering on anchor-selected paragraphs, under docs-write
  delete-bullets               Removes bullets while preserving prose and indentation, under docs-write
  text-style                   Sets explicit character formatting on an anchored range under docs-format
  paragraph-style              Styles whole paragraphs overlapping an anchored range under docs-format
  insert-table                 Inserts an empty table next to a body anchor, under docs-structure
  insert-table-row             Inserts one empty table row above/below a reference cell, under docs-structure
  insert-table-column          Inserts one empty table column left/right of a reference cell, under docs-structure
  delete-table-row             Removes one table row, under docs-table-delete; refuses the last row
  delete-table-column          Removes one table column, under docs-table-delete; refuses the last column
  create                       Creates a new Google Doc, optionally seeded with text. Gated by the write-permission rules' `create` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1615)
  create-named-range           Creates a scoped named-range label, gated by docs-structure
  delete-named-range           Deletes a scoped label by ID, leaving text intact; gated by docs-structure
  replace-named-range-content  Replaces a single named span by ID; docs-write, or docs-delete for empty text
  help                         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

