===== gwi drive docs paragraph-style =====
Styles whole paragraphs overlapping an anchored range under docs-format

Usage: gwi drive docs paragraph-style [OPTIONS] <--match <MATCH_TEXT>|--from <FROM>> <--alignment <ALIGNMENT>|--named-style <NAMED_STYLE>> <DOCUMENT_ID>

Arguments:
  <DOCUMENT_ID>
          Document id

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --match <MATCH_TEXT>
          One unique literal body match

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --from <FROM>
          Start of an inclusive anchored range

      --to <TO>
          End of an inclusive anchored range

      --ignore-case
          Match anchors using Unicode simple case folding

      --dry-run
          Report the resolved effect without writing

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

      --alignment <ALIGNMENT>
          Set paragraph alignment

          Possible values:
          - start:     Leading edge in the paragraph's writing direction
          - center:    Centered
          - end:       Trailing edge in the paragraph's writing direction
          - justified: Justified

      --named-style <NAMED_STYLE>
          Set a named paragraph style; may change inherited formatting

          Possible values:
          - normal-text: Ordinary prose
          - title:       Document title
          - subtitle:    Document subtitle
          - heading1:    Heading level one
          - heading2:    Heading level two
          - heading3:    Heading level three
          - heading4:    Heading level four
          - heading5:    Heading level five
          - heading6:    Heading level six

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi drive docs insert-table =====
Inserts an empty table next to a body anchor, under docs-structure

Usage: gwi drive docs insert-table [OPTIONS] --rows <ROWS> --columns <COLUMNS> <--before <BEFORE>|--after <AFTER>> <DOCUMENT_ID>

Arguments:
  <DOCUMENT_ID>
          Google document id

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --dry-run
          Resolve effects without mutating; does not authorize a subsequent write

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --ignore-case
          Match the literal anchor with Unicode simple case folding

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

      --before <BEFORE>
          Insert before this unique literal body anchor

      --after <AFTER>
          Insert after this unique literal body anchor

      --rows <ROWS>
          Positive row count; total grid is limited to 10000 cells

      --columns <COLUMNS>
          Positive column count

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

