===== gwi drive docs create =====
Creates a new Google Doc, optionally seeded with text. Gated by the write-permission rules' `create` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1615)

Usage: gwi drive docs create [OPTIONS] --name <NAME> --parent <FOLDER_ID>

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --name <NAME>
          The new document's title

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --parent <FOLDER_ID>
          The folder to create it in. Also what the permission gate evaluates

      --text <TEXT>
          Initial body text

      --text-file <PATH>
          Read the initial body text from a file, or `-` for stdin

      --dry-run
          Report what would happen without creating anything

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi drive docs create-named-range =====
Creates a scoped named-range label, gated by docs-structure

Usage: gwi drive docs create-named-range [OPTIONS] --tab <TAB> --segment <SEGMENT> --name <NAME> --start-index <START_INDEX> --end-index <END_INDEX> <DOCUMENT_ID>

Arguments:
  <DOCUMENT_ID>
          Document ID

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --tab <TAB>
          Server tab ID, or `legacy` for a response without tabs. Never defaults to first tab

      --segment <SEGMENT>
          `body` or an existing header/footer/footnote segment ID

      --dry-run
          Resolve and report the complete effect without mutation or a backup lease

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

      --name <NAME>
          Label, 1–256 UTF-16 units; names need not be unique

      --start-index <START_INDEX>
          Inclusive start in server UTF-16 units, inside one plain-text paragraph

      --end-index <END_INDEX>
          Exclusive end in server UTF-16 units; exclude the paragraph newline

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

