Changes workbook-level properties: locale, time zone, automatic recalculation, and iterative calculation. Gated by the folder write-permission rules' `sheets-structure` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1836)

Usage: gwi drive sheets update-workbook-properties [OPTIONS] <SPREADSHEET_ID>

Arguments:
  <SPREADSHEET_ID>
          Spreadsheet id (the /d/<ID>/ segment of a Sheets URL).

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --locale <LOCALE>
          The workbook's new locale, e.g. `en_US`. Omitted leaves it unchanged

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --time-zone <TIME_ZONE>
          The workbook's new IANA time zone, e.g. `America/New_York`. Omitted leaves it unchanged

      --auto-recalc <INTERVAL>
          The workbook's new automatic-recalculation interval. Omitted leaves it unchanged

          Possible values:
          - on-change: Recalculate on every edit (Sheets' own default)
          - minute:    Recalculate at most once a minute
          - hour:      Recalculate at most once an hour

      --iterative-calculation <ON_OFF>
          Turns iterative calculation on or off. Omitted leaves it unchanged

          Possible values:
          - on:  Turn iterative calculation on (or update its settings)
          - off: Turn iterative calculation off

      --iterative-calculation-max-iterations <N>
          Maximum calculation rounds per recalculation. Only valid alongside `--iterative-calculation on`; omitted takes Sheets' own default

      --iterative-calculation-convergence-threshold <THRESHOLD>
          The maximum change between two consecutive rounds that still counts as converged. Only valid alongside `--iterative-calculation on`; omitted takes Sheets' own default

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made, without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi drive sheets format-cells =====
Applies a cell format across a range. Gated by the folder write-permission rules' `sheets-structure` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1643)

Usage: gwi drive sheets format-cells [OPTIONS] <SPREADSHEET_ID>

Arguments:
  <SPREADSHEET_ID>
          Spreadsheet id (the /d/<ID>/ segment of a Sheets URL).

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --range <A1>
          A1 range to format, optionally carrying its own `Sheet!` prefix

      --sheet <NAME>
          Sheet (tab) title. Supplies the prefix for a bare `--range`

      --bold <BOOL>
          Bold
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --italic <BOOL>
          Italic
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --strikethrough <BOOL>
          Strikethrough
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --underline <BOOL>
          Underline
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --font-size <N>
          Point size

      --text-color <HEX>
          Text color, `#RRGGBB`

      --background <HEX>
          Cell background color, `#RRGGBB`

      --horizontal-align <ALIGN>
          Horizontal alignment
          
          [possible values: left, center, right]

      --vertical-align <ALIGN>
          Vertical alignment
          
          [possible values: top, middle, bottom]

      --number-format <PATTERN>
          Display number format pattern, e.g. `"#,##0.00"`. Requires `--number-format-type`

      --number-format-type <TYPE>
          The number format's type. Requires `--number-format`
          
          [possible values: text, number, percent, currency, date, time, date-time, scientific]

      --wrap <WRAP>
          Text wrap behavior
          
          [possible values: overflow, clip, wrap]

      --font-family <NAME>
          Font family name, e.g. `"Arial"`

      --text-rotation-angle <DEGREES>
          Rotation angle in degrees, -90 to 90. Mutually exclusive with `--text-rotation-vertical`

      --text-rotation-vertical
          Stack text vertically instead of rotating it. Mutually exclusive with `--text-rotation-angle`

      --hyperlink-display-type <TYPE>
          How a cell containing a hyperlink is displayed
          
          [possible values: linked, plain-text]

      --padding-top <N>
          Top padding, in pixels. Must be non-negative

      --padding-right <N>
          Right padding, in pixels. Must be non-negative

      --padding-bottom <N>
          Bottom padding, in pixels. Must be non-negative

      --padding-left <N>
          Left padding, in pixels. Must be non-negative

      --text-direction <DIR>
          Text direction
          
          [possible values: left-to-right, right-to-left]

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made, without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi drive sheets update-borders =====
Sets border lines on a range's edges. Gated by the folder write-permission rules' `sheets-structure` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1643)

Usage: gwi drive sheets update-borders [OPTIONS] <SPREADSHEET_ID>

Arguments:
  <SPREADSHEET_ID>
          Spreadsheet id (the /d/<ID>/ segment of a Sheets URL).

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --range <A1>
          A1 range to border, optionally carrying its own `Sheet!` prefix

      --sheet <NAME>
          Sheet (tab) title. Supplies the prefix for a bare `--range`

      --top
          Set the top edge

      --bottom
          Set the bottom edge

      --left
          Set the left edge

      --right
          Set the right edge

      --all
          Set all four edges. Equivalent to passing all of `--top`/`--bottom`/`--left`/`--right`. Does **not** include `--inner-horizontal`/`--inner-vertical`, which need to be named explicitly

      --inner-horizontal
          Set the horizontal grid lines between rows within the range

      --inner-vertical
          Set the vertical grid lines between columns within the range

      --style <STYLE>
          Line style, shared by every edge this call sets
          
          [default: solid]
          [possible values: solid, solid-medium, solid-thick, dashed, dotted, double]

      --color <HEX>
          Line color, `#RRGGBB`. Omitted takes solid black

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made, without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

