===== gwi drive sheets set-data-validation =====
Sets a data validation rule on a range. Gated by the folder write-permission rules' `sheets-structure` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1643).

Boxed (rust-works/omni-dev#1792): tranche 2's ~19 extra condition flags pushed this variant far past every sibling's size, which `clippy::large_enum_variant` flags transitively up through `SheetsSubcommands`/`DriveSubcommands`/ `Commands`.

Usage: gwi drive sheets set-data-validation [OPTIONS] <--one-of-list <A,B,C>|--one-of-range <A1_RANGE>|--number-between <MIN> <MAX>|--number-not-between <MIN> <MAX>|--number-greater <N>|--number-greater-eq <N>|--number-less <N>|--number-less-eq <N>|--number-eq <N>|--number-not-eq <N>|--text-contains <TEXT>|--text-not-contains <TEXT>|--text-starts-with <TEXT>|--text-ends-with <TEXT>|--text-eq <TEXT>|--date-after <DATE>|--date-before <DATE>|--date-on <DATE>|--date-between <START> <END>|--blank|--not-blank|--checkbox|--custom-formula <FORMULA>> <SPREADSHEET_ID>

Arguments:
  <SPREADSHEET_ID>
          Spreadsheet id (the /d/<ID>/ segment of a Sheets URL).

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --range <A1>
          A1 range to validate, optionally carrying its own `Sheet!` prefix

      --sheet <NAME>
          Sheet (tab) title. Supplies the prefix for a bare `--range`

      --one-of-list <A,B,C>
          Restrict entries to this comma-separated list (renders as a dropdown)

      --one-of-range <A1_RANGE>
          Restrict entries to a dropdown sourced from this range

      --number-between <MIN> <MAX>
          Restrict entries to a number in this inclusive range

      --number-not-between <MIN> <MAX>
          Restrict entries to a number outside this inclusive range

      --number-greater <N>
          Restrict entries to a number strictly greater than this

      --number-greater-eq <N>
          Restrict entries to a number greater than or equal to this

      --number-less <N>
          Restrict entries to a number strictly less than this

      --number-less-eq <N>
          Restrict entries to a number less than or equal to this

      --number-eq <N>
          Restrict entries to a number equal to this

      --number-not-eq <N>
          Restrict entries to a number not equal to this

      --text-contains <TEXT>
          Restrict entries to text containing this substring

      --text-not-contains <TEXT>
          Restrict entries to text not containing this substring

      --text-starts-with <TEXT>
          Restrict entries to text starting with this substring

      --text-ends-with <TEXT>
          Restrict entries to text ending with this substring

      --text-eq <TEXT>
          Restrict entries to text equal to this

      --date-after <DATE>
          Restrict entries to a date after this one. Absolute dates only — Sheets rejects a relative keyword like `today` in data validation (accepted in `add-conditional-format`/`update-conditional-format`, not here)

      --date-before <DATE>
          Restrict entries to a date before this one. Absolute dates only (see `--date-after`)

      --date-on <DATE>
          Restrict entries to a date equal to this one. Absolute dates only (see `--date-after`)

      --date-between <START> <END>
          Restrict entries to a date in this inclusive range (absolute dates only; relative keywords are not accepted here)

      --blank
          Restrict entries to an empty cell

      --not-blank
          Restrict entries to a non-empty cell

      --checkbox
          Restrict entries to `TRUE`/`FALSE`, rendered as a checkbox

      --custom-formula <FORMULA>
          Restrict entries to ones for which this formula evaluates truthy

      --input-message <TEXT>
          Tooltip text shown on the cell

      --show-warning
          Allow an invalid entry through with a warning, instead of rejecting it outright

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made, without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

