===== gwi drive sheets protect-range =====
Protects a range or an entire sheet. Gated by the folder write-permission rules' `sheets-protection` operation — distinct from `sheets-structure` (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1643)

Usage: gwi drive sheets protect-range [OPTIONS] <SPREADSHEET_ID>

Arguments:
  <SPREADSHEET_ID>
          Spreadsheet id (the /d/<ID>/ segment of a Sheets URL).

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --range <A1>
          A1 range to protect, optionally carrying its own `Sheet!` prefix. Mutually exclusive with `--whole-sheet`

      --sheet <NAME>
          Sheet (tab) title. Supplies the prefix for a bare `--range`, or the target sheet directly with `--whole-sheet`

      --whole-sheet
          Protect the entire sheet named by `--sheet`, rather than a range within it

      --description <TEXT>
          A human-readable note about why the range is protected

      --warning-only
          Only warn on an edit rather than blocking it outright

      --editor <EMAIL>
          An editor exempted from the protection. Repeatable

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made, without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi drive sheets update-protection =====
Changes an existing protected range's description, warning-only flag, or editor list. Gated by the folder write-permission rules' `sheets-protection` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1643)

Usage: gwi drive sheets update-protection [OPTIONS] <SPREADSHEET_ID>

Arguments:
  <SPREADSHEET_ID>
          Spreadsheet id (the /d/<ID>/ segment of a Sheets URL).

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --range <A1>
          A1 range identifying the existing protection, optionally carrying its own `Sheet!` prefix. Must match exactly — see `drive sheets list-protections`. Mutually exclusive with `--whole-sheet`

      --sheet <NAME>
          Sheet (tab) title. Supplies the prefix for a bare `--range`, or the target sheet directly with `--whole-sheet`

      --whole-sheet
          Target the whole-sheet protection on `--sheet`, rather than one covering a range within it — the only way to reach a protection created with `protect-range --whole-sheet`, which has no range of its own to match against

      --description <TEXT>
          The new description

      --warning-only <BOOL>
          The new warning-only flag
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --add-editor <EMAIL>
          An editor to add. Repeatable

      --remove-editor <EMAIL>
          An editor to remove. Repeatable

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made, without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

