===== gwi drive sheets add-conditional-format =====
Adds a conditional format rule to one or more ranges. Gated by the folder write-permission rules' `sheets-structure` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1793, ADR-0081 §1).

Boxed for the same `clippy::large_enum_variant` reason as `SetDataValidation` (rust-works/omni-dev#1792): the condition/gradient flag set is wide.

Usage: gwi drive sheets add-conditional-format [OPTIONS] --sheet <NAME> --range <A1> <--number-between <MIN> <MAX>|--number-not-between <MIN> <MAX>|--number-greater <N>|--number-greater-eq <N>|--number-less <N>|--number-less-eq <N>|--number-eq <N>|--number-not-eq <N>|--text-contains <TEXT>|--text-not-contains <TEXT>|--text-starts-with <TEXT>|--text-ends-with <TEXT>|--text-eq <TEXT>|--date-after <DATE>|--date-before <DATE>|--date-on <DATE>|--date-between <START> <END>|--cell-empty|--cell-not-empty|--custom-formula <FORMULA>|--gradient-min-color <HEX>> <SPREADSHEET_ID>

Arguments:
  <SPREADSHEET_ID>
          Spreadsheet id (the /d/<ID>/ segment of a Sheets URL).

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --sheet <NAME>
          Sheet (tab) title every `--range` belongs to

      --range <A1>
          An A1 range (no `Sheet!` prefix — `--sheet` supplies it) the rule applies to. Repeatable; at least one is required

      --index <N>
          Where to insert the rule, 0-based. Omit to append (the sheet's current rule count)

      --number-between <MIN> <MAX>
          Restrict the trigger to a number in this inclusive range

      --number-not-between <MIN> <MAX>
          Restrict the trigger to a number outside this inclusive range

      --number-greater <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number strictly greater than this

      --number-greater-eq <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number greater than or equal to this

      --number-less <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number strictly less than this

      --number-less-eq <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number less than or equal to this

      --number-eq <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number equal to this

      --number-not-eq <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number not equal to this

      --text-contains <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text containing this substring

      --text-not-contains <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text not containing this substring

      --text-starts-with <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text starting with this substring

      --text-ends-with <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text ending with this substring

      --text-eq <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text equal to this

      --date-after <DATE>
          Restrict the trigger to a date after this one. Accepts an absolute date or a relative keyword (`today`, `tomorrow`, `yesterday`, `past-week`, `past-month`, `past-year`)

      --date-before <DATE>
          Restrict the trigger to a date before this one. Accepts an absolute date or a relative keyword (see `--date-after`)

      --date-on <DATE>
          Restrict the trigger to a date equal to this one. Accepts an absolute date or a relative keyword (see `--date-after`)

      --date-between <START> <END>
          Restrict the trigger to a date in this inclusive range (absolute dates only; relative keywords are not accepted here)

      --cell-empty
          Trigger when the cell is empty

      --cell-not-empty
          Trigger when the cell is not empty

      --custom-formula <FORMULA>
          Trigger when this formula evaluates truthy

      --background <HEX>
          Cell background color to apply, `#RRGGBB`. Companion to a condition flag above, not part of the `rule_kind` group itself

      --text-color <HEX>
          Text color to apply, `#RRGGBB`

      --bold <BOOL>
          Bold text
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --gradient-min-color <HEX>
          Build a gradient instead: the color at the low end of the scale (anchored `MIN`), `#RRGGBB`. Requires `--gradient-max-color`

      --gradient-max-color <HEX>
          The color at the high end of the scale (anchored `MAX`), `#RRGGBB`

      --gradient-mid-color <HEX>
          An optional midpoint's color, `#RRGGBB`. Requires `--gradient-mid-type`/`--gradient-mid-value`

      --gradient-mid-type <TYPE>
          What kind of value the midpoint is anchored to

          Possible values:
          - number:     Anchored at an absolute cell value
          - percent:    Anchored at a percentage of the range's value spread
          - percentile: Anchored at a percentile of the range's values

      --gradient-mid-value <VALUE>
          The midpoint's threshold value, untouched — Sheets parses it at evaluation time

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made, without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

