      --number-greater-eq <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number greater than or equal to this

      --number-less <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number strictly less than this

      --number-less-eq <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number less than or equal to this

      --number-eq <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number equal to this

      --number-not-eq <N>
          Restrict the trigger to a number not equal to this

      --text-contains <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text containing this substring

      --text-not-contains <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text not containing this substring

      --text-starts-with <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text starting with this substring

      --text-ends-with <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text ending with this substring

      --text-eq <TEXT>
          Restrict the trigger to text equal to this

      --date-after <DATE>
          Restrict the trigger to a date after this one. Accepts an absolute date or a relative keyword (`today`, `tomorrow`, `yesterday`, `past-week`, `past-month`, `past-year`)

      --date-before <DATE>
          Restrict the trigger to a date before this one. Accepts an absolute date or a relative keyword (see `--date-after`)

      --date-on <DATE>
          Restrict the trigger to a date equal to this one. Accepts an absolute date or a relative keyword (see `--date-after`)

      --date-between <START> <END>
          Restrict the trigger to a date in this inclusive range (absolute dates only; relative keywords are not accepted here)

      --cell-empty
          Trigger when the cell is empty

      --cell-not-empty
          Trigger when the cell is not empty

      --custom-formula <FORMULA>
          Trigger when this formula evaluates truthy

      --background <HEX>
          Cell background color to apply, `#RRGGBB`. Companion to a condition flag above, not part of the `rule_kind` group itself

      --text-color <HEX>
          Text color to apply, `#RRGGBB`

      --bold <BOOL>
          Bold text
          
          [possible values: true, false]

      --gradient-min-color <HEX>
          Build a gradient instead: the color at the low end of the scale (anchored `MIN`), `#RRGGBB`. Requires `--gradient-max-color`

      --gradient-max-color <HEX>
          The color at the high end of the scale (anchored `MAX`), `#RRGGBB`

      --gradient-mid-color <HEX>
          An optional midpoint's color, `#RRGGBB`. Requires `--gradient-mid-type`/`--gradient-mid-value`

      --gradient-mid-type <TYPE>
          What kind of value the midpoint is anchored to

          Possible values:
          - number:     Anchored at an absolute cell value
          - percent:    Anchored at a percentage of the range's value spread
          - percentile: Anchored at a percentile of the range's values

      --gradient-mid-value <VALUE>
          The midpoint's threshold value, untouched — Sheets parses it at evaluation time

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made (including the rule currently at `--index`), without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

