===== gwi drive sheets add-chart =====
Adds a chart. Gated by the folder write-permission rules' `sheets-structure` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1797, ADR-0081 §3).

Boxed for the same `clippy::large_enum_variant` reason as `SetDataValidation` (rust-works/omni-dev#1792): the chart-spec flag set is wide.

Usage: gwi drive sheets add-chart [OPTIONS] --type <TYPE> --domain <A1> <SPREADSHEET_ID>

Arguments:
  <SPREADSHEET_ID>
          Spreadsheet id (the /d/<ID>/ segment of a Sheets URL).

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --type <TYPE>
          `column`, `bar`, `line`, `area`, `scatter`, or `pie`

      --domain <A1>
          The domain (category/x-axis) range, e.g. `A2:A10`. Must carry its own `Sheet!` prefix unless `--sheet` is given

      --series <A1>
          A data series range. Repeatable for a basic chart; a pie chart takes exactly one

      --sheet <NAME>
          Sheet title, supplying the prefix for `--domain`/`--series`/ `--anchor` when they don't carry their own

      --title <TITLE>
          The chart's title

      --subtitle <SUBTITLE>
          The chart's subtitle

      --legend <POSITION>
          `bottom`, `top`, `left`, `right`, or `none`

      --stacked <MODE>
          `none`, `stacked`, or `percent` — column/bar/area charts only

      --header-count <N>
          How many leading rows/columns of the source range are headers — basic charts only

      --horizontal-axis-title <HORIZONTAL_AXIS_TITLE>
          The horizontal axis title — basic charts only

      --vertical-axis-title <VERTICAL_AXIS_TITLE>
          The vertical axis title — basic charts only

      --pie-hole <0.0-1.0>
          `0.0`-`1.0` center-hole radius — pie charts only. `0.0` (or absent) is a solid pie.
          
          `allow_hyphen_values`: without it, a negative value (rejected by `validate_pie_hole` with a specific message) never reaches that check — clap's own arg parser rejects `--pie-hole -0.1` first with a confusing "unexpected argument '-0'" error, matching `conditional_format.rs`'s numeric flags for the same reason.

      --anchor <A1>
          The anchor cell, e.g. `E2`. Required unless `--new-sheet`

      --offset-x <PX>
          Additional horizontal offset from the anchor cell, in pixels

      --offset-y <PX>
          Additional vertical offset from the anchor cell, in pixels

      --width <PX>
          The chart's width in pixels

      --height <PX>
          The chart's height in pixels

      --new-sheet
          Put the chart on a brand-new sheet of its own, instead of anchoring it to an existing one. Cannot move or resize an existing chart — see the module docs' documented cuts

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made, without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi drive sheets update-chart =====
Replaces an existing chart's spec wholesale — `updateChartSpec` carries no field mask. Gated by the folder write-permission rules' `sheets-structure` operation (issue rust-works/omni-dev#1797, ADR-0081 §3)

Usage: gwi drive sheets update-chart [OPTIONS] --chart-id <ID> <SPREADSHEET_ID>

Arguments:
  <SPREADSHEET_ID>
          Spreadsheet id (the /d/<ID>/ segment of a Sheets URL).

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Drive account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Drive account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see ADR-0066, ADR-0069). Overrides `GWI_DRIVE_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `drive` subtree — not usable before the `drive` subcommand name, only after it, so it can't collide with an unrelated subcommand's own `--account` flag.

      --chart-id <ID>
          Which chart to update, discovered via `list-charts`

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

      --type <TYPE>
          Change the chart's type. Refused if it would switch between a basic chart and a pie chart — delete and re-add instead

      --domain <A1>
          Replace the domain range (requires `--series` too)

      --series <A1>
          Replace every series wholesale. Repeatable

      --sheet <NAME>
          Sheet title, supplying the prefix for `--domain`/`--series` when they don't carry their own

      --title <TITLE>
          Change the title

      --subtitle <SUBTITLE>
          Change the subtitle

      --legend <POSITION>
          Change the legend position

      --stacked <MODE>
          Change the stacking mode — basic charts only

      --header-count <N>
          Change the header row/column count — basic charts only

      --horizontal-axis-title <HORIZONTAL_AXIS_TITLE>
          Change the horizontal axis title — basic charts only

      --vertical-axis-title <VERTICAL_AXIS_TITLE>
          Change the vertical axis title — basic charts only

      --pie-hole <0.0-1.0>
          Change the pie-hole radius — pie charts only

      --dry-run
          Reports the gate verdict and the change that would be made, without calling `spreadsheets.batchUpdate`

      --lease <TOKEN>
          The lease token from `drive lease acquire`, required unless the deciding write-permission rule sets `require_lease: false` — a token presented anyway is still validated and consumed (ADR-0080 §1/§9/§13). Never needed with `--dry-run`

  -o, --output <OUTPUT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - table: Human-readable table
          - json:  JSON
          - yaml:  YAML (single document)
          - yamls: YAML stream (`---`-separated multi-document)
          - jsonl: JSON Lines: one compact JSON object per line, streaming-friendly
          
          [default: table]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

